1
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:42,320
You're the one who did this
to my father, aren't you?

2
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:44,320
Are you sure he's your father?

3
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:47,680
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Get the documents ready.</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">We'll take care of it tomorrow.</font></font></i>

4
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:50,520
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Thank you. Mother.</font></font></i>

5
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:54,240
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Ever since Phakorn came back from America</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">and moved in with you,</font></font></i>

6
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:55,520
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">it's been one thing after another.</font></font></i>

7
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:57,400
You really don't seem to trust Korn.

8
00:02:57,480 --> 00:03:00,400
Your brother hasn't exactly given me
a reason to trust him.

9
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:01,360
MR. PHAKORN TAYAWAT

10
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:04,000
Will you be my girlfriend?

11
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:05,920
Yes.

12
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:13,960
PHAKORN

13
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:16,520
Hey, Wee. Where are you? Who are you with?

14
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:20,160
I'm at a hospital in Chonburi.
I came to see Mr. Nimit.

15
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:23,320
Who are you with?
Alyssa isn't answering my calls.

16
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,560
Are you with her?

17
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:26,960
I'm alone right now.

18
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:10,480
If you need to cry, just cry.
You don't have to be strong all the time.

19
00:04:16,519 --> 00:04:18,240
It's okay to be weak sometimes.

20
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:21,399
Go ahead and cry. I won't make fun of you.

21
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:37,120
You know,

22
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:40,720
I really envy you and Korn.

23
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:43,840
You have each other to lean on.

24
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:47,920
I feel like

25
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:50,360
I'm all alone.

26
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:52,840
Like I have to fight everything by myself.

27
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,360
Then just think of me…

28
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:08,440
as a brother.

29
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:24,720
Sometimes I wish I'd been born a man.

30
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:27,160
Maybe I'd be stronger,

31
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:29,680
and Dad wouldn't have to worry so much.

32
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:14,800
Korn.

33
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:24,120
Korn!

34
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:26,120
Korn!

35
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:31,120
You said you were alone.
Why did you lie to me?

36
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:34,320
Just listen. I was alone at first.

37
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:36,040
I only ran into Ms. Alyssa just now.

38
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:37,880
Liar.

39
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,440
Listen to me, Korn.

40
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:42,800
Why would I lie to you?

41
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:45,080
If you want to know, ask Ms. Alyssa.

42
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:49,680
Korn!

43
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:52,680
Enough! Stop it!

44
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:57,040
What the hell is wrong with you?

45
00:06:58,440 --> 00:07:00,880
What the hell is wrong with you?
You're my girlfriend,

46
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:02,640
and you're hugging my brother?

47
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:04,440
She was upset and crying.

48
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:07,920
I was just comforting her.
Nothing else happened, Korn.

49
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,320
Is that really all?

50
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:13,120
That's all. Believe it or not,
it's up to you.

51
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:16,880
You keep pretending
you're on my side, Wee.

52
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:19,160
But you're waiting
to stab me in the back, aren't you?

53
00:07:21,320 --> 00:07:24,680
Or are you jealous
that I have a better life?

54
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:29,800
Why would I do that? When…

55
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:30,960
When what?

56
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:35,360
You know perfectly well
I'm not jealous of you.

57
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:53,120
Alyssa.

58
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:55,360
Alyssa.

59
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,640
Alyssa, please hear me out.

60
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:59,120
Get a grip, and then we can talk.

61
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:01,320
I'm exhausted.

62
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,160
I don't want to explain anything.

63
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:05,320
Think whatever you want.

64
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:07,800
But sort yourself out first.

65
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:10,040
Don't act like a mad dog again.

66
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:14,400
Okay, Alyssa.

67
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:17,080
I'm sorry. I lost my temper.

68
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:21,760
You have no idea
what I've been through today.

69
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:24,240
I'm so exhausted I could cry.

70
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:26,440
Mr. Rawee was just comforting me.

71
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:28,680
Why did you have to lose it?
I don't understand.

72
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:31,400
Because it was Wee.

73
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:36,360
I feel like I'm the one
who came between you and him.

74
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:40,760
You two are like exes
who went their separate ways,

75
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:43,080
then found each other again
and just clicked.

76
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:48,080
That's ridiculous.

77
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:51,680
Just tell me.

78
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:53,960
Is Wee the one you really want?

79
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:57,920
Is he why it took you so long
to give me a chance?

80
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:04,360
Is he, Alyssa? Answer me.

81
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:07,280
What if he is?

82
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:09,360
Are you going to step aside?

83
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:15,160
Do you still want to be together?

84
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:18,240
If not, we can end it.

85
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:21,240
Alyssa.

86
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:22,400
Alyssa.

87
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,600
I'm sorry.

88
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:26,440
I was wrong.

89
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:30,440
Can we please not break up?
Please, Alyssa.

90
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:32,200
Don't say we're done again.

91
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:34,320
I'm sorry.

92
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,400
Please.

93
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:43,520
Please, Alyssa.

94
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:42,840
Yes?

95
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:45,440
You can take my car back.

96
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:48,800
I'll have Korn drive me to my dad's.

97
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:50,800
Okay.

98
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:53,680
Thank you for today.

99
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:56,280
And I'm sorry

100
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:58,640
I caused you and your brother to fight.

101
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:40,480
Mr. Rawee was just comforting me.

102
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:42,720
Why did you have to lose it?
I don't understand.

103
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:45,440
Because it was Wee.

104
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:50,440
I feel like I'm the one
who came between you and him.

105
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:54,800
You two are like exes
who went their separate ways,

106
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:57,120
then found each other again
and just clicked.

107
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,800
-What is it?
-Mr. Phakorn is in trouble.

108
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:33,400
Mr. Panas reported to the board
that Phakorn embezzled 20 million.

109
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:36,120
Where is Phakorn now?

110
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:41,760
RAWEE

111
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,680
MOTHER

112
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:10,760
Hello.

113
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:13,160
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Where are you?</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Why aren't you at the office?</font></font></i>

114
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:17,000
I have a client meeting this afternoon.

115
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:20,640
You still need to come in
before your meeting.

116
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:22,400
What kind of executive are you?

117
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:24,680
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You're not working here part-time.</font></font></i>

118
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:26,640
Wait.

119
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:30,160
What are you so mad about? Calm down, Mom.

120
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:32,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Get to the office right now.</font></font></i>

121
00:13:32,160 --> 00:13:33,760
We need to discuss something important.

122
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:36,320
Have Taddao postpone your client meeting.

123
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:39,160
Okay.

124
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:51,920
EXPENSE DISBURSEMENT REPORT

125
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:57,040
Mr. Panas must've set Korn up.

126
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:59,040
Please help him, Ms. Nada.

127
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:02,280
He'd never cheat the company.

128
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:04,360
He'd never steal from the company.

129
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:05,960
Rawee.

130
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:09,040
Phakorn isn't the same person anymore.

131
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:11,880
Unless you're blind and deaf,

132
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:15,280
you should know how much he's changed.

133
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:18,800
Should I get Mr. Phakorn?

134
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:21,320
Yes. Go get him.

135
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,280
Yes, ma'am.

136
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:42,320
You wanted to see me, Mom?

137
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:51,280
Explain.

138
00:14:53,920 --> 00:14:55,680
Well…

139
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:59,240
If you can't explain it,

140
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:02,680
then tell me the truth.
What did you do with all the money?

141
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:09,280
Forget about everyone else.

142
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:12,240
You need to tell me the truth, Korn.

143
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,040
Otherwise,

144
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:16,480
no one here can help you.

145
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:18,600
The board already knows everything.

146
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:21,320
They're going to call you in soon.

147
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:42,760
I thought Nimit would send Thamrong.

148
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:50,080
Dad isn't the one who wanted to see you.

149
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:53,400
I am. I just asked him
to set up the meeting.

150
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:57,160
What do you want?

151
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:02,200
I want you to sign an agreement.

152
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:05,080
If I take care of the resort,

153
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:07,600
you'll stay out of our company for good.

154
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:11,160
This is the last thing
you'll get from Dad.

155
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,280
Who do you think you are,

156
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:16,800
deciding what to do
with the family assets?

157
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:25,400
They're not family assets.

158
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:27,240
They're Dad's.

159
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:31,840
Grandpa already divided the family assets
equally between you and Dad.

160
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:35,680
Everything that's left belongs to Dad.

161
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:39,360
And I'm his only legal heir.

162
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:58,160
This pen is a great brand.

163
00:16:58,240 --> 00:17:01,520
It writes smoothly.
You can use it for writing.

164
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:03,640
Or…

165
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,560
even signing for your inheritance
from your father.

166
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:18,119
Go ahead and sign it.

167
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:21,680
Your pen still works pretty well.

168
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:23,520
It's been a while, hasn't it?

169
00:17:24,119 --> 00:17:26,040
I've been saving it for this moment.

170
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:50,040
Wow.

171
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,960
You signed without even reading it.

172
00:17:56,120 --> 00:17:57,880
What if the deal isn't in your favor?

173
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:03,960
From now on,

174
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:06,920
stay away from Dad and our company.

175
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,880
Otherwise, I'll sue
to take everything back.

176
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:14,600
You can start getting the paperwork ready
on Tawan Island.

177
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:19,920
See you there.

178
00:18:30,520 --> 00:18:33,320
Still as arrogant as ever, you damn brat.

179
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:44,600
So the 20 million you withdrew

180
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:46,280
was for marketing?

181
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:48,480
Yes, Mr. Sumet.

182
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:51,680
Our wellness project
is still very new in Thailand,

183
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:54,240
so we want a strong marketing campaign.

184
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:56,880
That's why we decided to hire
an outside PR firm.

185
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:58,840
So where's this PR team

186
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:01,160
you're talking about?

187
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:03,840
You've already withdrawn the money.

188
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,800
You must've hired someone, right?

189
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:09,160
Where's the proof?

190
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:13,960
Not yet. We haven't hired anyone.

191
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:16,360
We're still hearing pitches
before we decide.

192
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:19,080
I understand Phakorn

193
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,160
may have skipped a few steps.

194
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:23,840
He's impatient.

195
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:25,880
He didn't want to wait
for the money or the deal,

196
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:29,960
so he went ahead with it.
You know how ambitious young people are.

197
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:34,280
Then return the money
to the company for now.

198
00:19:34,360 --> 00:19:36,240
Once you've chosen a team,

199
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:39,680
you can withdraw it again.
It's not too late, is it?

200
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:47,400
I'm willing to follow
the board's decision.

201
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:54,800
Here's a check for the 20 million.

202
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:57,120
If you'd like me to return it for now,

203
00:19:57,720 --> 00:19:58,640
I will.

204
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:04,960
But either way, I'll need
to withdraw it again in a few weeks.

205
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:15,560
In that case,
there's no need to return it.

206
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:17,800
I thought this was something urgent.

207
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:21,040
I knew Ms. Nada's son

208
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:23,200
wouldn't cheat or embezzle
from the company.

209
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:25,080
It's only 20 million.

210
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:27,800
What a waste of everyone's time.

211
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:29,560
Please, sit down.

212
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:32,320
Not at all.

213
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,200
We're happy to clear things up.

214
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:39,240
But this is nothing

215
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:41,840
like when Mr. Panas

216
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:44,720
used company money
for his personal investments.

217
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:53,240
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Why did you do this?</font></font></i>

218
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:55,360
You're the one who told me to invest.

219
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:56,960
Why did you betray me?

220
00:20:58,200 --> 00:21:01,960
Keep your voice down, kid.
The whole company will find out

221
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:03,120
what an idiot you are.

222
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:05,600
What?

223
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:08,560
You're gonna hit me? Go ahead.

224
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:09,960
Hit me.

225
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:12,680
Then I can charge you with assault too.

226
00:21:12,760 --> 00:21:16,360
What? Let all hell break loose.

227
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:18,040
Come on.

228
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:24,440
I respected you like family.
Why the hell did you do this?

229
00:21:25,280 --> 00:21:29,080
Damn, you really are an idiot.

230
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:32,680
Who'd consider someone
from a mistress's family one of us?

231
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:37,480
You got lucky this time.

232
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:39,360
But next time,

233
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:42,920
I promise I'll make it even worse for you.

234
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:48,560
See you around.

235
00:22:17,240 --> 00:22:20,000
Hold on, Mr. Panas!
Mr. Panas, please wait!

236
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:26,680
Yes, ma'am.

237
00:22:29,040 --> 00:22:30,160
What is it?

238
00:22:32,920 --> 00:22:36,160
Your son's not nearly as good as you.

239
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:43,080
He might get away with it this time.

240
00:22:45,440 --> 00:22:46,920
But if there's a next time,

241
00:22:47,720 --> 00:22:49,360
he won't be so lucky.

242
00:22:55,480 --> 00:22:57,400
So you've finally shown your true colors.

243
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:01,560
I wonder

244
00:23:01,640 --> 00:23:03,800
how Mrs. Wasana raised her children.

245
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:06,000
You and Pim

246
00:23:06,680 --> 00:23:08,400
are exactly alike.

247
00:23:11,320 --> 00:23:14,320
This is ridiculous. Are you kidding me?

248
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:19,240
But it is funny. Really funny.

249
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:22,480
Yeah, laugh all you want.

250
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:26,280
Once I get serious, you'll be sorry.

251
00:23:28,560 --> 00:23:31,640
I'm terrified. Absolutely terrified.

252
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:34,880
Thanks for serving that up.

253
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:38,720
Now get ready for my return.

254
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:41,720
What should I take this time?

255
00:23:42,720 --> 00:23:45,400
Your position or

256
00:23:46,440 --> 00:23:47,560
the whole company?

257
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:50,040
You bitch, Nada!

258
00:23:50,120 --> 00:23:51,920
What are you gonna do about it, Panas?

259
00:24:15,040 --> 00:24:16,040
Sit down.

260
00:24:25,760 --> 00:24:27,080
Excuse me.

261
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:30,640
Taddao asked me to bring you some coffee.

262
00:24:36,080 --> 00:24:37,160
Thank you.

263
00:24:39,960 --> 00:24:42,120
I'm taking you off this project, Korn.

264
00:24:45,840 --> 00:24:46,880
Mom.

265
00:24:48,240 --> 00:24:49,880
If you stay on it,

266
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:51,960
Panas will find another way
to come after us.

267
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:53,680
Go work on something else for now.

268
00:24:55,360 --> 00:24:58,320
But that's no different from firing me.

269
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:00,360
Would you rather I fire you?

270
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:03,360
If you still don't know
what you did wrong,

271
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:05,240
go think long and hard about it.

272
00:25:05,320 --> 00:25:08,360
It cost a lot to save that brain of yours.

273
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:10,680
Learn to use it instead of your emotions.

274
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:30,960
Where's Taddao?

275
00:25:31,040 --> 00:25:32,520
She went to Accounting.

276
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:37,880
You don't need to help Phakorn anymore.

277
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:40,840
Go back to helping
Taddao and me like before.

278
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:42,800
Why?

279
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:47,920
Tell Taddao I'm going to visit Father.

280
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:49,080
I won't be coming back to the office.

281
00:25:50,280 --> 00:25:51,080
And thank you

282
00:25:51,760 --> 00:25:54,760
for today, Rawee.
Your idea really helped Phakorn.

283
00:25:56,280 --> 00:25:57,400
Ms. Nada.

284
00:25:58,880 --> 00:26:00,160
Um…

285
00:26:01,160 --> 00:26:02,880
Could I take a couple of days off?

286
00:26:03,520 --> 00:26:04,760
Where are you going?

287
00:26:05,920 --> 00:26:07,280
Tawan Island.

288
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:09,920
What are you going there for?

289
00:26:10,680 --> 00:26:12,240
I have some business there for Mr. Nimit.

290
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:15,000
What is it? Can you tell me?

291
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:18,360
Mr. Nimit is selling
the resort to Mr. Jak.

292
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:23,120
And what does that have to do with you?

293
00:26:23,760 --> 00:26:26,840
Mr. Nimit asked me to help Ms. Alyssa
look over the contract.

294
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:28,480
What about Mr. Thamrong?

295
00:26:29,360 --> 00:26:30,440
He's going too.

296
00:26:33,520 --> 00:26:36,680
Alright. Tell Taddao

297
00:26:36,760 --> 00:26:38,680
I've approved your leave.

298
00:26:39,720 --> 00:26:40,800
Thank you very much.

299
00:27:01,080 --> 00:27:02,600
Hi, Dad.

300
00:27:08,640 --> 00:27:09,760
How are you feeling?

301
00:27:14,840 --> 00:27:16,120
Where's Aunt Pat?

302
00:27:17,600 --> 00:27:19,320
She went home to get some things.

303
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:22,680
Alright.

304
00:27:24,280 --> 00:27:27,640
Alyssa, Rawee promised me

305
00:27:27,720 --> 00:27:29,400
he'd go with you.

306
00:27:30,360 --> 00:27:32,080
But I'm sending Thamrong along too.

307
00:27:33,640 --> 00:27:35,520
Then who's going to take care of you?

308
00:27:36,120 --> 00:27:37,960
Your Aunt Pat.

309
00:27:38,040 --> 00:27:41,920
There are doctors and nurses here too.
Don't worry about me.

310
00:27:50,360 --> 00:27:52,120
Rawee is a good man.

311
00:27:55,080 --> 00:27:57,120
If you need to cry, just cry.

312
00:27:57,200 --> 00:27:58,880
You don't have to be strong all the time.

313
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:06,600
It's okay to be weak sometimes.

314
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:09,800
Go ahead and cry. I won't make fun of you.

315
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:13,160
Then just think of me

316
00:28:14,920 --> 00:28:17,040
as an older brother.

317
00:28:29,880 --> 00:28:33,440
Sometimes I wish I'd been born a man.

318
00:28:34,200 --> 00:28:35,720
Maybe I'd be stronger,

319
00:28:36,360 --> 00:28:38,520
and Dad wouldn't have to worry so much.

320
00:28:56,400 --> 00:28:58,720
He's almost too good, actually.

321
00:29:00,840 --> 00:29:03,520
So where do things stand
with you and Phakorn?

322
00:29:08,360 --> 00:29:11,200
If you're not serious about him yet…

323
00:29:13,280 --> 00:29:15,120
I'd like you

324
00:29:15,800 --> 00:29:17,880
to give Rawee a chance.

325
00:29:19,320 --> 00:29:22,560
If it's Rawee,
I won't have to worry about you.

326
00:29:25,280 --> 00:29:27,560
You sound like
you're going somewhere soon.

327
00:29:28,400 --> 00:29:31,200
You'll be around to worry about me
for a long time yet.

328
00:29:32,880 --> 00:29:34,480
I'm just saying for the future.

329
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:40,440
I can take care of myself, you know.

330
00:29:41,320 --> 00:29:43,480
I don't need anyone to look after me.

331
00:29:45,600 --> 00:29:47,920
I'm your father. Of course, I worry.

332
00:29:49,680 --> 00:29:52,480
Have you talked to Rawee
about the trip yet?

333
00:30:03,720 --> 00:30:06,080
Who's calling? Is it Rawee?

334
00:30:06,760 --> 00:30:09,200
PHAKORN

335
00:30:12,680 --> 00:30:14,800
I'll go take this call.

336
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:27,280
Hello, Aunt Pat.

337
00:30:27,360 --> 00:30:29,240
Hello. Come on in.

338
00:30:31,880 --> 00:30:33,240
Hello, Uncle.

339
00:30:33,320 --> 00:30:35,880
Sorry it took me so long to visit.

340
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:39,160
That's alright.
I didn't tell anyone anyway.

341
00:30:41,200 --> 00:30:42,360
How's your mother?

342
00:30:42,440 --> 00:30:46,320
She's been pretty busy lately,
so she asked me to visit you for her.

343
00:30:46,400 --> 00:30:47,720
Thank you.

344
00:30:48,720 --> 00:30:50,840
And what's all this you brought?

345
00:30:51,680 --> 00:30:53,400
Here.

346
00:30:53,480 --> 00:30:54,600
Thank you.

347
00:30:54,680 --> 00:30:56,360
I picked these out myself. I don't know

348
00:30:56,440 --> 00:30:58,240
if you and Aunt Pat will like them.

349
00:30:58,320 --> 00:31:00,120
Oh my!

350
00:31:00,200 --> 00:31:02,400
These are all such nice things. Thank you.

351
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:04,160
You're welcome.

352
00:31:04,240 --> 00:31:05,520
Oh, Alyssa.

353
00:31:05,600 --> 00:31:08,840
I was going to tell you
I'm not going to Tawan Island anymore.

354
00:31:08,920 --> 00:31:12,360
I'm staying here to take care of him.

355
00:31:12,960 --> 00:31:15,960
But Thamrong's going
with you anyway, right?

356
00:31:20,080 --> 00:31:22,720
I was just about to tell you
you don't need to come.

357
00:31:23,560 --> 00:31:25,280
Please take care of Dad for me.

358
00:31:25,920 --> 00:31:26,840
Of course.

359
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:30,440
You're going to Tawan Island? What for?

360
00:31:33,360 --> 00:31:34,640
I have some business for Dad.

361
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:38,040
Then why don't I go with you?

362
00:31:38,120 --> 00:31:39,560
No need.

363
00:31:40,160 --> 00:31:41,760
Rawee's already going with her.

364
00:31:47,320 --> 00:31:50,040
I need Mr. Rawee
to look over some documents.

365
00:31:50,120 --> 00:31:52,560
We need someone with some legal knowledge.

366
00:31:55,520 --> 00:31:57,440
Ask me again.

367
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:01,640
Will you be my girlfriend?

368
00:32:12,360 --> 00:32:13,400
Yes.

369
00:32:21,760 --> 00:32:23,560
Alyssa probably hasn't told you yet,
has she?

370
00:32:30,160 --> 00:32:31,400
Alyssa and I…

371
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:34,920
are together now.

372
00:32:42,920 --> 00:32:44,160
Really?

373
00:32:46,920 --> 00:32:49,360
Oh my goodness. Alyssa!

374
00:32:53,120 --> 00:32:55,280
I was just about to tell everyone.

375
00:32:58,240 --> 00:33:00,720
Then let me go to the island too.

376
00:33:00,800 --> 00:33:02,760
I can be a good boyfriend.

377
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:05,840
Don't worry, Uncle.

378
00:33:06,440 --> 00:33:08,840
I'll take good care of Alyssa.

379
00:33:27,160 --> 00:33:28,800
Can I be a little upset?

380
00:33:30,120 --> 00:33:31,640
About what?

381
00:33:32,840 --> 00:33:35,640
You haven't told anyone we're together.

382
00:33:37,120 --> 00:33:38,480
I haven't had a chance.

383
00:33:41,240 --> 00:33:43,040
I know you're still mad at me.

384
00:33:45,880 --> 00:33:47,880
Have you apologized to Mr. Rawee yet?

385
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:54,600
Something came up at the company.
I haven't had a chance to talk to Wee yet.

386
00:33:54,680 --> 00:33:56,040
What happened?

387
00:34:01,280 --> 00:34:02,720
I got tricked.

388
00:34:07,760 --> 00:34:11,320
I didn't really want to tell you.
It makes me look stupid.

389
00:34:11,920 --> 00:34:13,920
I don't want you to think I'm stupid.

390
00:34:17,840 --> 00:34:19,639
Not knowing something
doesn't make you stupid.

391
00:34:22,520 --> 00:34:25,320
You didn't actually take any money
from the company, did you?

392
00:34:28,960 --> 00:34:32,400
No, Alyssa. I used my own money.

393
00:34:34,719 --> 00:34:38,120
I guess Uncle Panas
already had it in for Mom and me,

394
00:34:38,199 --> 00:34:39,360
so he made the whole thing up.

395
00:34:41,880 --> 00:34:43,320
But it still hurts.

396
00:34:43,400 --> 00:34:45,679
He doesn't even consider me family.

397
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:52,639
But do you really consider him family?

398
00:34:53,360 --> 00:34:54,320
Of course.

399
00:34:54,920 --> 00:34:58,400
I felt reassured
when he started being nice to me.

400
00:34:59,280 --> 00:35:02,280
Maybe because Aunt Pim never accepted me.

401
00:35:02,360 --> 00:35:05,320
So it felt good
to have someone on my side.

402
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:12,720
So what are you going to do now?

403
00:35:16,400 --> 00:35:17,680
Nothing.

404
00:35:18,360 --> 00:35:20,200
Mom will probably take care of it.

405
00:35:23,600 --> 00:35:24,800
Aunt Da's amazing, isn't she?

406
00:35:27,360 --> 00:35:29,160
Uh, Alyssa.

407
00:35:30,040 --> 00:35:32,560
How long have you known Aunt Da?

408
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:35,880
As long as I can remember.

409
00:35:36,440 --> 00:35:38,960
Aunt Da is Dad's closest female friend.

410
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:42,480
But she's always been
the same Aunt Da, right?

411
00:35:44,560 --> 00:35:45,520
What do you mean?

412
00:35:46,680 --> 00:35:48,440
I mean,

413
00:35:48,520 --> 00:35:50,680
she has always been

414
00:35:50,760 --> 00:35:52,400
this beautiful, right?

415
00:35:55,480 --> 00:35:57,160
Pretty much.

416
00:35:58,560 --> 00:35:59,680
Maybe even prettier.

417
00:35:59,760 --> 00:36:02,120
Back then, she had a sweet, proper look.

418
00:36:02,720 --> 00:36:04,720
Now she looks much more sophisticated.

419
00:36:04,800 --> 00:36:06,520
Maybe it's just because she's older.

420
00:36:15,080 --> 00:36:16,800
-Here. Thank you.
-Of course.

421
00:36:26,120 --> 00:36:27,680
Oh, Aunt Walai. Hello.

422
00:36:27,760 --> 00:36:29,120
Hello.

423
00:36:29,200 --> 00:36:31,160
Oh, Mom.

424
00:36:31,240 --> 00:36:33,440
Why didn't you tell me
you were visiting Uncle Nimit?

425
00:36:33,520 --> 00:36:34,760
I could've picked you up.

426
00:36:35,760 --> 00:36:38,840
My car broke down,
so I couldn't work today.

427
00:36:38,920 --> 00:36:41,560
I thought I'd make Mr. Nimit
some rice porridge instead.

428
00:36:41,640 --> 00:36:44,400
I didn't know you'd be here.
I would've made some for you too.

429
00:36:45,240 --> 00:36:46,600
That's alright.

430
00:36:48,640 --> 00:36:49,640
Dad.

431
00:36:50,400 --> 00:36:54,080
I'm going back to Bangkok
to get some things.

432
00:36:56,800 --> 00:36:58,200
Then I'll drive you.

433
00:36:58,280 --> 00:36:59,560
Won't you take your mother home?

434
00:37:00,880 --> 00:37:02,000
It's alright.

435
00:37:02,080 --> 00:37:04,640
I can get a ride home. It's not far.

436
00:37:04,720 --> 00:37:08,080
Phakorn, since you're already home,

437
00:37:08,160 --> 00:37:09,960
stay the night with your mother.

438
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:12,040
She misses you.

439
00:37:15,720 --> 00:37:16,600
Ms. Alyssa.

440
00:37:17,200 --> 00:37:18,640
I can drive you.

441
00:37:19,400 --> 00:37:20,720
It's alright.

442
00:37:20,800 --> 00:37:23,360
I'd rather you stay here with Dad.

443
00:37:26,120 --> 00:37:27,840
Can I borrow your car?

444
00:37:28,880 --> 00:37:31,840
Wee already took my car back to Bangkok.

445
00:37:32,480 --> 00:37:35,320
Of course. But are you sure
you'll be okay driving alone?

446
00:37:35,840 --> 00:37:37,200
No problem.

447
00:37:39,120 --> 00:37:40,160
Excuse me, sir.

448
00:37:50,040 --> 00:37:51,280
See you.

449
00:38:10,080 --> 00:38:13,160
I think Mr. Nimit and Mr. Thamrong
definitely don't like me.

450
00:38:14,840 --> 00:38:16,360
Why do you think that?

451
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:18,920
Maybe they already know the truth,

452
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:20,680
that I'm not Ms. Nada's son.

453
00:38:22,320 --> 00:38:23,640
But I don't care.

454
00:38:24,160 --> 00:38:26,320
I'm a Tayawat now.

455
00:38:29,600 --> 00:38:31,920
You're using the Tayawat name now?

456
00:38:32,680 --> 00:38:34,240
How did that happen?

457
00:38:35,480 --> 00:38:37,720
I guess they wanted to make it official.

458
00:38:37,800 --> 00:38:39,560
It matters when it comes to inheritance.

459
00:38:43,320 --> 00:38:46,120
And how is Mr. Prajak doing?

460
00:38:46,800 --> 00:38:48,640
Have you been to see him?

461
00:38:55,640 --> 00:38:57,760
Is there a chance
Father will wake up soon?

462
00:38:59,360 --> 00:39:01,240
It's 50-50, Ms. Nada.

463
00:39:01,320 --> 00:39:03,600
If he'd gotten to the hospital sooner,

464
00:39:03,680 --> 00:39:05,840
his chances would've been as high as 90%.

465
00:39:06,400 --> 00:39:10,040
But Mr. Prajak
is responding well to treatment.

466
00:39:12,280 --> 00:39:14,120
You don't need to worry.

467
00:39:14,200 --> 00:39:16,920
We'll take the best possible care of him.

468
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:20,600
Please take good care of him, Doctor.

469
00:39:21,880 --> 00:39:25,480
You know my father's all I have left.

470
00:39:26,560 --> 00:39:27,400
Of course.

471
00:39:29,000 --> 00:39:30,280
Thank you.

472
00:40:09,880 --> 00:40:11,120
Oh no.

473
00:40:13,120 --> 00:40:14,520
What happened here?

474
00:40:18,080 --> 00:40:19,840
KANJANAPISEK TAXI COOPERATIVE LIMITED

475
00:40:27,840 --> 00:40:30,960
Mr. Rawee!

476
00:40:32,440 --> 00:40:33,760
Mr. Rawee!

477
00:40:51,960 --> 00:40:55,280
If you have something to say,
just say it. It's late.

478
00:40:57,240 --> 00:40:58,480
Okay.

479
00:40:59,680 --> 00:41:02,000
You're coming to Tawan Island
with me, right?

480
00:41:02,800 --> 00:41:03,880
Yes.

481
00:41:04,440 --> 00:41:06,160
I already promised your father.

482
00:41:07,240 --> 00:41:08,200
Okay.

483
00:41:09,120 --> 00:41:11,720
I just came back
to get some important documents.

484
00:41:11,800 --> 00:41:13,280
I'll see you there.

485
00:41:16,120 --> 00:41:19,120
And I'm sorry about that night.

486
00:41:19,200 --> 00:41:22,040
I didn't mean to cause
a fight between you and Korn.

487
00:41:24,760 --> 00:41:26,760
After we're done on Tawan Island,

488
00:41:27,720 --> 00:41:28,920
let's not stay in touch anymore.

489
00:41:29,520 --> 00:41:30,720
What do you mean?

490
00:41:31,760 --> 00:41:33,520
I mean,

491
00:41:33,600 --> 00:41:35,880
let's go back to being strangers.

492
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:38,000
Why?

493
00:41:39,600 --> 00:41:41,320
I don't want Korn
to get the wrong idea again.

494
00:41:42,640 --> 00:41:43,560
Uh…

495
00:41:44,160 --> 00:41:47,240
Are you pretending not to know,
or do you really not know

496
00:41:47,840 --> 00:41:49,920
how I actually feel about Korn?

497
00:41:52,480 --> 00:41:53,440
I don't want to know.

498
00:41:54,280 --> 00:41:56,880
Even if I might be using your brother?

499
00:41:57,760 --> 00:41:59,920
What are you using
my brother for this time?

500
00:42:01,720 --> 00:42:02,680
Maybe

501
00:42:03,480 --> 00:42:06,800
to find Aunt Da's real son.

502
00:42:18,840 --> 00:42:20,280
You like me, don't you?

503
00:42:22,360 --> 00:42:24,720
You keep coming around
and using this as an excuse.

504
00:42:25,640 --> 00:42:27,880
You did all this
because you like me, didn't you?

505
00:42:31,040 --> 00:42:32,400
What if I said I do?

506
00:42:34,680 --> 00:42:36,760
Then I'd tell you
I don't feel the same way.

507
00:42:41,400 --> 00:42:44,880
Stop judging who's right and who's wrong.

508
00:42:45,800 --> 00:42:49,200
There's more to it
than you think you know.

509
00:42:53,040 --> 00:42:55,640
How's your father?

510
00:42:58,000 --> 00:42:59,160
He's okay.

511
00:42:59,760 --> 00:43:01,840
He's being discharged tomorrow.

512
00:43:05,720 --> 00:43:08,920
If that's all, I'll be going.

513
00:43:11,320 --> 00:43:12,840
Okay, Wee.

514
00:43:13,440 --> 00:43:14,640
Don't call me that again.

515
00:43:15,520 --> 00:43:17,880
Well, you're the one

516
00:43:17,960 --> 00:43:20,560
who told me to think of you
as an older brother.

517
00:43:21,280 --> 00:43:23,800
-Call me what you did before.
-Okay, Wee.

518
00:43:39,320 --> 00:43:40,600
Jerk.

519
00:43:54,720 --> 00:43:56,200
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You like me, don't you?</font></font></i>

520
00:43:56,280 --> 00:43:58,640
You keep coming around
and using this as an excuse.

521
00:43:59,560 --> 00:44:01,800
You did all this
because you like me, didn't you?

522
00:44:02,400 --> 00:44:03,720
What if I said I do?

523
00:44:04,800 --> 00:44:06,880
Then I'd tell you
I don't feel the same way.

524
00:44:10,680 --> 00:44:12,120
If that's all,

525
00:44:12,720 --> 00:44:13,840
I'll be going.

526
00:44:16,200 --> 00:44:17,320
Okay, Wee.

527
00:44:18,360 --> 00:44:19,560
Don't call me that again.

528
00:44:20,360 --> 00:44:22,800
Well, you're the one

529
00:44:22,880 --> 00:44:25,480
who told me to think of you
as an older brother.

530
00:44:26,160 --> 00:44:28,480
-Call me what you did before.
-Okay, Wee.

531
00:45:02,000 --> 00:45:03,320
I'm not selling it.

532
00:45:04,640 --> 00:45:06,760
That house holds too many memories.

533
00:45:10,960 --> 00:45:13,080
No matter how painful they are,

534
00:45:14,120 --> 00:45:15,760
I'm keeping it.

535
00:45:16,280 --> 00:45:18,080
I understand, Lada.

536
00:45:18,800 --> 00:45:21,160
But I'd like you to think it over again.

537
00:45:21,760 --> 00:45:24,680
Alright. I'll think about it.

538
00:45:25,360 --> 00:45:27,120
Thank you for letting me know.

539
00:45:41,080 --> 00:45:42,080
Mr. Nimit.

540
00:45:42,720 --> 00:45:46,240
I found out who's buying our resort.

541
00:45:46,320 --> 00:45:48,960
-Who?
-MP Phithak.

542
00:45:49,040 --> 00:45:50,960
I've checked everything. We can trust him.

543
00:45:54,240 --> 00:45:55,440
Mr. Nimit.

544
00:45:56,320 --> 00:45:59,240
Rawee doesn't really need to go with us.

545
00:46:00,960 --> 00:46:03,080
I want Rawee to look over the agreement.

546
00:46:03,160 --> 00:46:05,200
I'm worried Jak might try something again.

547
00:46:07,680 --> 00:46:10,040
You're not trying

548
00:46:10,120 --> 00:46:11,840
to set Ms. Alyssa up with Rawee, are you?

549
00:46:13,440 --> 00:46:14,800
You know

550
00:46:14,880 --> 00:46:16,680
she's dating Phakorn.

551
00:46:18,920 --> 00:46:22,480
To be honest,
I don't trust Phakorn at all.

552
00:46:23,920 --> 00:46:26,200
So he's using the Tayawat name now, right?

553
00:46:27,720 --> 00:46:28,760
Yes.

554
00:46:33,600 --> 00:46:34,800
Where have you been?

555
00:46:42,840 --> 00:46:44,240
I went to visit Mr. Nimit.

556
00:46:45,560 --> 00:46:47,200
I'm going to Tawan Island tomorrow.

557
00:46:50,560 --> 00:46:51,440
Why?

558
00:46:54,440 --> 00:46:55,280
That's my business.

559
00:46:56,120 --> 00:46:58,200
Let's talk about us instead.

560
00:47:00,600 --> 00:47:03,760
You might not know this,
but there's still a way

561
00:47:03,840 --> 00:47:06,280
to prove that Wee
is his biological grandson.

562
00:47:06,960 --> 00:47:08,920
The two of us aren't that safe yet.

563
00:47:10,240 --> 00:47:11,480
Who told you?

564
00:47:12,720 --> 00:47:14,320
I called the lab and asked.

565
00:47:19,760 --> 00:47:21,840
And is it true Grandfather

566
00:47:22,440 --> 00:47:23,400
changed his will?

567
00:47:26,520 --> 00:47:27,360
Yes.

568
00:47:29,000 --> 00:47:30,160
So what's your plan?

569
00:47:31,920 --> 00:47:33,360
That's my business.

570
00:47:41,800 --> 00:47:43,080
-Alright.
-Thank you.

571
00:47:43,160 --> 00:47:44,200
Of course.

572
00:47:48,640 --> 00:47:51,600
Packing at the crack of dawn?

573
00:47:51,680 --> 00:47:54,560
You look pretty excited to go.

574
00:47:55,640 --> 00:47:57,400
Who'd be excited to see Uncle Jak?

575
00:47:57,480 --> 00:47:59,960
I just want to get my packing over with.

576
00:48:02,240 --> 00:48:04,000
I can't go with you,

577
00:48:04,080 --> 00:48:06,240
so take good care of yourself, okay?

578
00:48:06,960 --> 00:48:08,440
Don't worry.

579
00:48:09,960 --> 00:48:13,520
With that Rawee going too,
I'm even more worried.

580
00:48:15,880 --> 00:48:19,080
Why are you still so biased against Wee?

581
00:48:21,000 --> 00:48:22,480
Wee?

582
00:48:27,000 --> 00:48:30,480
I think I should pack
something with long sleeves too.

583
00:48:30,560 --> 00:48:31,960
The sun's really strong.

584
00:48:49,440 --> 00:48:50,280
MS. ALYSSA: SEE YOU THERE, WEE

585
00:48:57,040 --> 00:48:59,640
-I'LL DRIVE MYSELF. SEE YOU THERE, WEE
-OKAY, LET'S DO THAT

586
00:49:15,760 --> 00:49:17,680
Have a safe trip.

587
00:49:18,800 --> 00:49:22,080
Please take care of Dad for me.
Call me if anything comes up.

588
00:49:22,160 --> 00:49:24,240
Don't worry about that.

589
00:49:26,360 --> 00:49:29,040
Take good care of yourself, okay?
I'm worried about you.

590
00:49:29,120 --> 00:49:31,600
-Okay. I'm off.
-Alright.

591
00:49:51,920 --> 00:49:56,440
FRESH COFFEE

592
00:50:33,080 --> 00:50:34,000
Hello.

593
00:50:36,520 --> 00:50:37,640
What are you doing here?

594
00:50:40,600 --> 00:50:42,360
I forgot to tell you.

595
00:50:42,920 --> 00:50:44,400
Korn's coming with us.

596
00:50:50,640 --> 00:50:54,360
Mr. Nimit asked me to help Ms. Alyssa
look over the Tawan Island sale agreement.

597
00:50:56,360 --> 00:50:57,600
I know.

598
00:50:57,680 --> 00:51:00,760
Mr. Nimit seems to trust you a lot, Wee.

599
00:51:04,680 --> 00:51:07,040
We should get going.
The resort car is waiting.

600
00:51:11,760 --> 00:51:13,200
Give me Alyssa's bags.

601
00:51:23,200 --> 00:51:24,880
I'll take care of my girlfriend.

602
00:51:53,560 --> 00:51:54,440
Let's go.

603
00:52:02,760 --> 00:52:04,760
Hello, my dear niece.

604
00:52:06,120 --> 00:52:07,640
This is Phakorn, Ms. Nada's son.

605
00:52:08,240 --> 00:52:09,080
-Hello.
-And this is Rawee.

606
00:52:09,160 --> 00:52:10,880
He's my lawyer.

607
00:52:15,200 --> 00:52:16,560
Welcome.

608
00:52:16,640 --> 00:52:19,840
The staff are cleaning the rooms.
You'll have to wait a bit.

609
00:52:20,880 --> 00:52:21,960
Are there fewer guests right now?

610
00:52:24,400 --> 00:52:26,200
We're fully booked all the time.

611
00:52:27,000 --> 00:52:29,040
With this many of you showing up,

612
00:52:29,120 --> 00:52:30,960
you're lucky I managed
to find rooms for you.

613
00:52:32,440 --> 00:52:33,600
Wow.

614
00:52:33,680 --> 00:52:36,200
Business is this good
and you still want to sell?

615
00:52:38,680 --> 00:52:40,280
We'll take whatever rooms you have.

616
00:52:41,640 --> 00:52:43,600
As long as there's a bed.
It's only one night.

617
00:52:45,160 --> 00:52:47,560
Three adjoining rooms in the garden wing.

618
00:52:48,240 --> 00:52:49,840
Then Wee can share a room with me.

619
00:52:50,440 --> 00:52:51,920
But it's a single bed.

620
00:52:53,080 --> 00:52:56,360
We've shared a bed since we were kids.
That's no problem.

621
00:52:58,520 --> 00:53:00,520
Okay. This way, please.

622
00:53:27,120 --> 00:53:28,640
Which side do you want?

623
00:53:30,640 --> 00:53:32,000
You choose, Wee.

624
00:53:46,680 --> 00:53:48,400
Are you still mad at me?

625
00:53:51,800 --> 00:53:53,480
I was never mad at you.

626
00:53:54,240 --> 00:53:57,400
Aren't you the one who was mad at me?

627
00:54:00,240 --> 00:54:02,240
Alyssa explained everything to me.

628
00:54:04,080 --> 00:54:06,000
You listen when she talks,

629
00:54:06,080 --> 00:54:07,560
but not when I do.

630
00:54:09,000 --> 00:54:11,080
-Wee…
-Forget it.

631
00:54:12,880 --> 00:54:14,720
Once this is over,

632
00:54:14,800 --> 00:54:16,440
I won't get involved with her anymore.

633
00:54:17,440 --> 00:54:18,800
You can stop worrying.

634
00:54:20,040 --> 00:54:22,280
-Why?
-Korn,

635
00:54:23,280 --> 00:54:25,840
if Dad knew we fought over a woman,

636
00:54:25,920 --> 00:54:27,400
he'd really let us have it.

637
00:54:32,560 --> 00:54:35,240
I'm sorry I punched you, Wee.

638
00:54:36,240 --> 00:54:38,800
It's okay. It didn't hurt.

639
00:54:43,400 --> 00:54:46,200
I'm going for a walk.
Want to come with me?

640
00:54:47,880 --> 00:54:51,360
No, thanks. I'm going
to rest my eyes for a bit.

641
00:56:39,240 --> 00:56:41,360
SUN SECRETS RESORT, TAWAN ISLAND

642
00:57:15,720 --> 00:57:17,280
You're not going anywhere.

643
00:57:17,360 --> 00:57:18,680
Let go of me, Mr. Jak.

644
00:57:18,760 --> 00:57:19,560
Let go!

645
00:57:19,640 --> 00:57:21,880
You have a sister, don't you?

646
00:57:21,960 --> 00:57:23,360
Are you crazy?

647
00:57:24,560 --> 00:57:26,800
Ms. Nada, come out and talk to me!

648
00:57:34,160 --> 00:57:36,280
You already knew Ms. Nada was here?

649
00:57:36,880 --> 00:57:38,520
You don't seem surprised at all.

650
00:57:41,000 --> 00:57:43,080
Having dinner without inviting me?

651
00:57:43,720 --> 00:57:44,960
We didn't invite you

652
00:57:45,040 --> 00:57:47,240
because we don't want you at our table.

653
00:57:48,000 --> 00:57:49,520
Why is that so hard to understand?

654
00:57:52,440 --> 00:57:54,440
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Is there anything you want to tell me?</font></font></i>

655
00:57:55,320 --> 00:57:56,920
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I tell you everything.</font></font></i>

656
00:57:57,000 --> 00:57:59,960
Except your DNA test results with Aunt Da.

657
00:58:02,160 --> 00:58:03,960
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You got yourself into this mess,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">so fix it.</font></font></i>

658
00:58:04,640 --> 00:58:06,880
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">But as a friend, I just want to warn you.</font></font></i>

659
00:58:06,960 --> 00:58:08,880
Don't let this go any further.

660
00:58:11,240 --> 00:58:13,200
What if the truth comes out?

661
00:58:13,280 --> 00:58:14,480
I'll take responsibility.

662
00:58:15,080 --> 00:58:16,640
How can you possibly do that, Wee?

663
00:58:17,800 --> 00:58:19,160
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I'll take all the blame.</font></font></i>

664
00:58:19,240 --> 00:58:20,200
Wee!

665
00:58:20,280 --> 00:58:21,200
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You don't have to worry.</font></font></i>

666
00:59:00,600 --> 00:59:03,200
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
